Section: Inputs

 The anchor set is built ONCE and threaded, because a list constant is
 rebuilt at every mention and these are five certificates to parse.

  anchors : List X509Anchor = ta-anchors 0

  chain : List X509Cert = wc-parse-both

  wc-parse-both : List X509Cert
  wc-parse-both =
    when x509-parse w-leaf
      is None -> []
      is Just (l) -> wc-with-leaf l

  wc-with-leaf : X509Cert -> List X509Cert
  wc-with-leaf (l) =
    when x509-parse w-inter
      is None -> []
      is Just (i) -> [l, i]

 www.digicert.com in ASCII, which is what a certificate holds.

  host : List Integer =
    [119, 119, 119, 46, 100, 105, 103, 105, 99, 101, 114, 116, 46, 99, 111, 109]

  other-host : List Integer =
    [119, 119, 119, 46, 101, 120, 97, 109, 112, 108, 101, 46, 99, 111, 109]

 Inside the leaf's window, and long after it.

  now-ok : List Integer = [50, 48, 50, 54, 48, 56, 48, 49, 48, 48, 48, 48, 48, 48]
  now-late : List Integer = [50, 48, 51, 48, 48, 49, 48, 49, 48, 48, 48, 48, 48, 48]

Section: Every Anchor Must Be Able To Verify

 A root that PARSES is not a root that can be used, and the supplied/parsed
 line cannot tell them apart. Both P-384 roots parsed perfectly well for
 the whole time they were deliberately kept out of the anchor set: X509
 typed their keys KeyEcdsaOther and x509-can-verify answered False, so an
 anchor holding either would have counted as parsed and matched nothing.

 So this counts the anchors that can actually verify a signature. Add a
 root whose curve this tree does not implement and it parses, it counts,
 and only this line moves.

  usable : List X509Anchor, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  usable (as) (i) (n) =
    if i >= list-length as then n
    else usable-step as i n (list-at as i)

  usable-step : List X509Anchor, Integer, Integer, X509Anchor -> Integer
  usable-step (as) (i) (n) (a) =
    if x509-can-verify (a.xa-key) then usable as (i + 1) (n + 1)
    else usable as (i + 1) n

Section: Reporting

  verdict : X509Verdict -> Text
  verdict (v) =
    when v
      is ChainOk -> "Ok"
      is ChainEmpty -> "Empty"
      is ChainNotYetValid -> "NotYetValid"
      is ChainExpired -> "Expired"
      is ChainBadTime -> "BadTime"
      is ChainBadSignature -> "BadSignature"
      is ChainBrokenIssuer -> "BrokenIssuer"
      is ChainIssuerNotCa -> "IssuerNotCa"
      is ChainIssuerCannotSign -> "IssuerCannotSign"
      is ChainNoAnchor -> "NoAnchor"
      is ChainTooLong -> "TooLong"
      is ChainWrongIdentity -> "WrongIdentity"

Section: Body

 One positive and three negatives, and each negative changes exactly one
 thing: the name, the clock, the anchors.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("anchors supplied = " & show (ta-anchor-count 0) & ", parsed = " & show (list-length anchors))
    print-line-uni ("anchors that can verify = " & show (usable anchors 0 0))
    print-line-uni ("chain parsed = " & show (list-length chain))
    print-line-uni ("verify www.digicert.com = " & verdict (x509-verify-peer chain anchors now-ok host))
    print-line-uni ("wrong hostname = " & verdict (x509-verify-peer chain anchors now-ok other-host))
    print-line-uni ("clock in 2030 = " & verdict (x509-verify-peer chain anchors now-late host))
    print-line-uni ("no anchors = " & verdict (x509-verify-peer chain [] now-ok host))
  end

